    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d766">

                <pb facs="0799" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg485"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-08">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 8, 1914, noon</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Yours, August 7, noon. The bill in question does not cover the subject of the
                    transfer of the ships of belligerents to citizens of the <pb facs="0800" n="486"
                        xml:id="pg486"/> United States but deals only with the subject of American
                    registry and removes the restriction on ships over five years old and authorizes
                    President to dispense by proclamation with regulation confining watch officers
                    to American citizens, survey and measurement of ships.</p>
                <p>The transfer of the ships of belligerents to neutrals during hostilities is not
                    touched by the bill and will be governed by the principles of international law
                    and usage as heretofore.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
